<section class="service-page-intro">
  <div><p class="eyebrow">Presentation design</p><h2>More than a better-looking set of slides.</h2></div>
  <div class="prose"><p>A presentation has to work as an argument, a live experience and often a document that will be circulated afterwards. We help establish the purpose, identify the central message and build a sequence that gives each idea the right amount of space.</p><p>That can mean working from a rough collection of notes, restructuring an existing deck or developing a complete presentation from reports, interviews and data. Design begins once the communication problem is understood—not before.</p></div>
</section>

<section class="section-shell service-offers">
  <div class="split-heading"><h2>Presentation support for demanding contexts<span class="red-stop">.</span></h2><p>The level of help can range from structure and visual direction to complete PowerPoint-native production and handover.</p></div>
  <div class="service-offer-grid">
    <article><span>01</span><h3>Board and leadership</h3><p>Decision-focused presentations that distinguish the central argument from the detail needed to support it.</p></article>
    <article><span>02</span><h3>Research and policy</h3><p>Briefings that preserve the integrity of evidence while creating a clear route through complex findings.</p></article>
    <article><span>03</span><h3>Strategy and change</h3><p>Sequences, frameworks and roadmaps that help people understand a direction, programme or transformation.</p></article>
    <article><span>04</span><h3>Reusable systems</h3><p>Editable templates, chart styles and slide patterns that teams can use without losing clarity or consistency.</p></article>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="service-practical">
  <div><p class="eyebrow">What the work can include</p><h2>From source material to a presentation ready to use.</h2></div>
  <ul class="service-checklist"><li>Content review and narrative structure</li><li>Message hierarchy and slide planning</li><li>Charts, diagrams and visual explanation</li><li>PowerPoint-native design and animation</li><li>Speaker-led and leave-behind versions</li><li>Templates, quality assurance and handover</li></ul>
</section>

